<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Angles on the circle of a constant angle locus</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Points \(P\) on the major arc \(AB\) of a circle with centre \(O\) all have angle \(APB = {@th@}^{\circ}\). \(Q\) is on the minor arc.</p><p>(a)</p><div>Angle \(AOB = \) [[input:ans1]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b)</p><div>Angle \(AQB = \) [[input:ans2]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) \(R\) is on the same side of \(AB\) as \(P\), [[if test="is(sw=0)"]]inside[[else]]outside[[/if]] the circle. Is angle \(ARB\) greater than, equal to or less than \({@th@}^{\circ}\)?</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) The angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference: angle \(AOB = {@2*th@}^{\circ}\).</p><p>(b) \(APBQ\) is a cyclic quadrilateral, so its opposite angles add to \(180^{\circ}\): angle \(AQB = 180^{\circ} - {@th@}^{\circ} = {@180-th@}^{\circ}\).</p><p>(c) The arc is the locus of points that see \(AB\) at exactly \({@th@}^{\circ}\). [[if test="is(sw=0)"]]A point inside the circle, on the same side as the arc, is nearer to \(AB\) and sees it at a larger angle: angle \(ARB\) is greater than \({@th@}^{\circ}\).[[else]]A point outside the circle, on the same side as the arc, is further from \(AB\) and sees it at a smaller angle: angle \(ARB\) is less than \({@th@}^{\circ}\).[[/if]]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: angles on the circle of a constant angle locus. theta 25 to 85 in steps of 5, not 45 or 60 (two diagnostics coincide). sw 0: R inside the circle; 1: outside. Source: original. */
th: rand([25,30,35,40,50,55,65,70,75,80,85]);
sw: rand(2);
o3: [["eq",false,sconcat("equal to \\(",th,"^\\circ\\)")],["gt",is(sw=0),sconcat("greater than \\(",th,"^\\circ\\)")],["lt",is(sw=1),sconcat("less than \\(",th,"^\\circ\\)")]];
ta3: if is(sw=0) then "gt" else "lt";
wr3: if is(sw=0) then "lt" else "gt";]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>th={@th@}, sw={@sw@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Loci: angles on the circle of a constant angle locus</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.3: Use the angle at the centre and the cyclic quadrilateral with a constant angle locus, and decide whether a point inside or outside sees a larger or smaller angle.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is original to this project.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
